{
 "title": "Replication Spec - Analysis of Contagion in China's Stock Market: A Hawkes Process Perspective",
 "hypothesis": "Market and sector indices exhibit self-excitation / cross-excitation and sector rotation detectable via multivariate (non)linear Hawkes processes. Trading-day returns are transformed into point processes of extreme up/down events defined by quantile thresholds.",
 "data_sources": [
  "not stated - daily return series of Shanghai Composite (SSE), Shenzhen Component (SZI), ChiNext (GEI) - source not stated",
  "not stated - daily return series of CSI Consumer 000932, CSI Healthcare 000933, CSI Finance & Real Estate 000934 - source not stated"
 ],
 "sample": "Experiment 1: daily returns of Shanghai Composite, Shenzhen Component, ChiNext transformed into bivariate event sequences {t_i,d_i} where d_i=0 sharp rise (return >= 90th percentile) and d_i=1 sharp decline (return <=10th percentile). Thresholds computed per index history. Experiment 2: CSI Consumer, Healthcare, Fin&RE daily returns transformed into 6-type event sequences (0:cons-up,1:med-up,2:fin-up,3:cons-down,4:med-down,5:fin-down) using same quantile convention. Timeline segmented into 15 periods of 150 trading days. Goodness-of-fit sample: homogeneous Poisson vs Hawkes on 2013.02-2022.03 train and 2022.03-2023.03 test split. Sample sizes are count claims: shanghai_count, shenzhen_count, chinext_count, train_size, val_size, csi_consumer_count, csi_healthcare_count, csi_finre_count.",
 "period_start": "February 26, 2013",
 "period_end": "March 2023",
 "method": [
  "1. Obtain daily returns in percent for each index. Base normalized to 1.0 on February 26, 2013 for cumulative plots.",
  "2. For each index compute its 10th and 90th percentiles of its return history. Experiment 1 thresholds: Shanghai [-1.285, 1.481] %, Shenzhen [-1.701, 1.891] %, ChiNext [-2.105, 2.502] % - parameter claims shanghai_quant10, shanghai_quant90 etc. Define event at time t_i = trading-day index of extreme return; type d_i=0 if return >= q90 (sharp rise), d_i=1 if return <= q10 (sharp decline). This yields bivariate sequence {(t_i,d_i)} on [0,T] with T=2452 trading days.",
  "3. Split sequence 85% training (2084 samples, count claim train_size) and 15% validation (368 samples, count claim val_size) - as printed.",
  "4. Specify exponential kernel Hawkes for m=2: lambda_k*(t)= mu_k + sum_{j=1..m} sum_{t_i<t} alpha_{k,j} * omega * exp(-omega*(t-t_i)), mu_k>0, alpha>0. Set decay omega as hyperparameter, grid-searched; omega=0.1 for Shanghai, Shenzhen, ChiNext (parameter claims omega_shanghai, omega_shenzhen, omega_chinext). Estimate mu=[mu0,mu1] and impact matrix A=[alpha_{k,j}] by MLE: L(theta;T)= prod_i lambda_{d_i}*(t_i) * exp(-sum_j Lambda_j(T)), log L = sum_i log lambda_{d_i}*(t_i) - sum_j int_0^T lambda_j*(s) ds, using Python tick module. Same specification applied to each index separately.",
  "5. Experiment 2: Use CSI sector indices March 2013-March 2023, Count 2452 each. Segment timeline into 15 periods (parameter claim num_periods) each 150 trading days (parameter claim trading_days_per_period). Following previous convention define 2 event types per sector => m=6 types: 0 cons-up,1 med-up,2 fin-up,3 cons-down,4 med-down,5 fin-down.",
  "6. Specify nonlinear Hawkes with inhibition: lambda*(t)=g(overline{lambda}*(t)), overline{lambda}*(t)= mu + alpha*omega*exp(-omega*t), mu in R, alpha in R, omega>0, link g(x)=max(x,0.01) (parameter claim link_threshold=0.01). Remove non-negativity constraints on mu and A to allow inhibition. Estimate via SGD Monte Carlo MLE (Algorithm 1): int_0^T lambda_j*(s) ds = T * E_s[lambda_j*(s)], s~U(0,T), sample N uniform times T_m=[t_1..t_N], compute I_m = (sum_i lambda_m*(t_i)/N)*T, NLL = -sum_{t_i in H(t)} log lambda_{d_i}*(t_i) + sum_j I_m, backprop update.",
  "7. Focus estimation on Period 3: 2014.12 to 2015.08 (structural bull, high activity) and Period 5: 2016.03 to 2016.11 (pessimistic, low activity). Report 6x6 influence matrix A_{i,j} (estimate claims period3_A00..period3_A55, period5_A00..period5_A55), background intensity mu vector of length 6 (period3_mu0..period3_mu5, period5_mu0..period5_mu5) and decay omega (period3_omega, period5_omega). Interpret 6x6 block as [A B; C D] where A=up-trend, B=oversold rebound, C=pullback, D=down-trend.",
  "8. Goodness-of-fit Random Time Change Theorem: if lambda*(t)>0 and Lambda(T)=int_0^T lambda*(s) ds <inf, then {Lambda(t_i)} is unit-rate Poisson. Test by Q-Q plot of Delta Lambda(t_i)=Lambda(t_i)-Lambda(t_{i-1}) vs Exp(1) and scatter plot (Lambda_{t+1}-Lambda_t, Lambda_t-Lambda_{t-1}) for independence. Baseline homogeneous Poisson with moment estimator lambda_hat = 1 / (sum_i Delta t_i / n). Estimated lambda_train=[0.100,0.101] for 2013.02-2022.03 and lambda_test=[0.067,0.082] for 2022.03-2023.03 (estimate claims lambda_train_type0 etc). No numeric test statistic or p-value printed - visual assessment only. Stability condition rho(A)<1 mentioned as theoretical benchmark, no numeric estimate printed."
 ],
